# ── Private job-search data ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# These accumulate REAL data (companies, recruiters, contacts, outcomes) as you
# use the skills, so they are git-ignored by default — your real tracker and any
# generated analysis reports stay local and never reach a public repo. The
# safe-to-commit fictional reference is references/applications.example.md.
references/applications.md
references/pattern-analysis-*.md

# Any file you rename with a .local.md suffix is kept out of git — use this for a
# personal copy of any skeleton below that you don't want committed.
*.local.md

# If you fork PUBLICLY and fill these skeletons with your real background, either
# move to a PRIVATE fork or uncomment the lines below to keep them out of git:
# references/YOUR_PROFILE.md
# references/CUSTOMIZATION_MEMORY.md
# references/STRATEGIC_GAP_ASSESSMENT.md
# skills/resume-customizer/references/star-stories.md
# skills/resume-customizer/references/detailed-context.md
